# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local environment. Copy to .env.local — never commit .env.local.
#
# All three variables below are written automatically the first time you run
# `npx convex dev`. You should not need to fill them in by hand.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key — NOT in this file.
#
# The assistant runs in a Convex action (convex/agent/chat.ts), which executes
# on Convex's servers. `process.env` inside it reads the Convex deployment's
# environment, not this machine's, so a key in .env.local would never reach it.
#
# Set it on the deployment instead:
#
#     npx convex env set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY <key>
#
# Check it with `npx convex env list`. The assistant logs which credential
# answered, e.g. `[assistant] auth mode: api_key`.
#
# Note this differs from README.md, which says to put the key in .env.local.
# NOTES.md explains why that cannot work here.
#
# Never expose the key to the browser — anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is
# shipped to the client and can be spent by anyone who opens devtools.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
